<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<inkscape-extension xmlns="http://www.inkscape.org/namespace/inkscape/extension">
    <name>Axonometric Projection</name>
    <id>org.markus.architecture.axo_projection</id>

    <param name="tab" type="notebook">
        <page name="opts" gui-text="Options">
            <param name="mode" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="Projection:">
                <option value="side">Flat → side face y-z (horizontal becomes y)</option>
                <option value="top">Flat → top face x-y (upwards becomes y)</option>
                <option value="side_inv">Side face y-z → flat (undo)</option>
                <option value="top_inv">Top face x-y → flat (undo)</option>
            </param>
            <param name="pivot" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="Fixed joint line (selection bbox):">
                <option value="auto">Auto (side: left edge, top: bottom edge)</option>
                <option value="left">Left edge</option>
                <option value="right">Right edge</option>
                <option value="bottom">Bottom edge</option>
                <option value="top">Top edge</option>
            </param>
            <separator/>
            <param name="use_grid" type="bool"
                   gui-text="Align to document axonometric grid (angle + foreshortening)">false</param>
            <label appearance="header">Tripod (used only when NOT aligning to the grid)</label>
            <param name="lx" type="float" min="0.001" max="10000.0" precision="3"
                   gui-text="x length (per reference length):">80.0</param>
            <param name="ly" type="float" min="0.001" max="10000.0" precision="3"
                   gui-text="y length (same reference length):">35.66</param>
            <param name="angle" type="float" min="0.0" max="89.9" precision="3"
                   gui-text="y angle to horizontal (°):">35.0</param>
        </page>
        <page name="help" gui-text="Help">
            <label xml:space="preserve">Draw a face flat (true shape, x/z scale) next to
the edge it belongs to, select it (paths or groups),
then run this extension.

Side face: strip drawn to the RIGHT of a vertical
edge. Its horizontal extent becomes the depth y
(foreshortened by y/x, at the y angle); verticals
stay. The left bbox edge stays in place.

Top face: strip drawn ABOVE a horizontal edge. Its
upward extent becomes the depth y; horizontals stay.
The bottom bbox edge stays in place.

The matrix is prepended to each selected object's
transform (stroke widths are not compensated).
Ungrouping later pushes it down to the children.
"Undo" modes apply the inverse matrix.

Default tripod: x 80 / 0°, y 35.66 / 35°, z = x scale.

Align to document axonometric grid: reads the
grid's depth angle (gridanglez for the side face,
gridanglex for the top) and sets the foreshortening
to 1/sin(angle), so one drawing-unit of depth rises
exactly one grid row and corners land on the grid.
Draw the flat face with the same unit as the grid's
Spacing Y. Needs an Axonometric grid in the document
(File &gt; Document Properties &gt; Grids).</label>
        </page>
    </param>

    <effect>
        <object-type>all</object-type>
        <effects-menu>
            <submenu name="Architecture"/>
        </effects-menu>
    </effect>

    <script>
        <command location="inx" interpreter="python">axo_projection.py</command>
    </script>
</inkscape-extension>
